oofem.out
3D periodic lattice — SFRC cube, random ft, steel fibres bridging the crack
NonLinearStatic nmsteps 1 nsteps 100 contextOutputStep 1000 nmodules 2 profileopt 1
nsteps 100 rtolv 1.e-3 reqIterations 100 stiffMode 1 manrmsteps 10 maxiter 200 controllmode 0 stepLength 1.e-6 minsteplength 1.e-6 maxrestarts 0 hpcmode 2 hpc 2 #@CTLNODE 32 hpcw 1 1. donotfixload
vtkxmllattice primvars 1 1 cellvars 9 138 139 140 156 157 158 52 46 103 tstep_step 5 domain_all cross 1 crossstep 1
gpexportmodule vars 2 46 139 tstep_all
domain 3dLattice
OutputManager tstep_step 1 dofman_output {#@CTLNODE}
ncrosssect 3 nmat 3 nbc 2 nic 0 nltf 2 nset 0
latticecs 1 material 1
latticecs 2 material 2 shape 1 radius 0.0002
latticecs 3 material 3
# Concrete: scalar damage, ft randomised via random.dat
latticedamage 1 d 2400. talpha 0. e 30.e9 e0 100.e-6 wf 40.e-6 coh 2. ec 10. stype 3 randvars 1 800 randgen 1 2
# Steel fibre: linear elastic, circular cross-section (radius set in LatticeCS 2)
latticelinearelastic 2 d 7850. talpha 0. em 200.e9 nu 0.3
# Matrix-to-fibre bond: latticeslip with MC2010-style values for ribbed steel
latticeslip 3 d 0. talpha 0. e 200.e9 a1 1 a2 1 t0 4.e6 type 1 s1 1.e-5 alpha 0.5
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 prescribedvalue 0.0
NodalLoad 2 loadTimeFunction 1 Components 6 0. 1. 0. 0. 0. 0.
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1.
InterpolatingFunction 2 name random.dat dim 3
#%BEGIN_CHECK%
#NODE number #@CTLNODE dof 32 unknown d
#LOADLEVEL
#TIME
#%END_CHECK%
